  "surprise": "Systems mechanism half-confirmed, score unchanged, kept by the rule for the throughput. Token-budget length-sorted batches (18,432 padded tokens per step, 1,132 batches per epoch as predicted) ran 5,261/5,581/5,288 pretraining steps vs 136-fable's 3,370/3,351/3,367 (+56/+67/+57%, 57/54/57 ms per step vs 89), below the registered 5,500-9,000 on two seeds: fitting step = fixed + per-token to the two points (89 ms at ~51k padded tokens, 57 ms at 18.3k) gives ~39 ms of fixed per-step cost and ~1 ms per 1k tokens, so padding was ~55% of the incumbent's step and the remaining step is now ~70% fixed overhead (launches, the 30-matrix Muon loop, AdamW, the 15 s val pass) that 146-fable's batched Newton-Schulz barely touched; CUDA graphs or fewer launches are the next speed lead, worth up to ~2x on top of this. Metric 650/681/645 (exact mean 658.67) vs 655/673/646 (658.00): +0.67, paired -5/+8/-1, inside the registered -20..+60 but far below the central +22, i.e. noise around an unchanged score. Surprise 1: the extra 60% of steps (4.65/4.93/4.68 epochs, 715k-759k records seen vs 431k) overfit this 155k-record cap-6 set: val loss bottomed at 0.0786/0.0800/0.0790 at 195/90/135 s and then rose to 0.0881/0.0839/0.0841 at 300 s (136 final: 0.086/0.083/0.079; predicted 0.066-0.082, falsified), while train loss fell to ~0.03-0.05 (136: ~0.055); held-out greedy after pretraining 0.9685/0.963/0.972 (136: 0.965/0.9705/0.968) did not move. Surprise 2: the handed-off model was a much worse round-1 sampler: targets solved 273/408/264 (136: 577/529/662; predicted 560-720, falsified), sample acc 0.076/0.109/0.080 (136: 0.137/0.135/0.210), round-1 Lean parse failures 57/52/51% of 48,000 (136: 44/48/34%), whole-run parse-fail 26.8/20.1/25.4% vs 136's 17.0% and both-ok samples 289k vs 314k (-8%). Expert iteration then climbed faster than ever (r1->r4 +870/+757/+843 vs 136's +525/+585/+462) to round-4 1143/1165/1107 (mean 1138 vs 136's 1113, +25, the highest RL-solved count under the Lean protocol), but the eval transfer ratio dropped (eval/round-4 0.569/0.585/0.583 vs 0.594/0.604/0.575), so the net is zero: >=10 89/108/96 (mean 97.7 vs 102.7), >=11 17/25/18 (20.0 vs 22.3), >=12 3/5/4 (4.0 vs 3.7), L* 11/12/11, final held-out greedy 0.989/0.9905/0.9925; totals 1556/1629/1526 s (136: 1517/1549/1616). Reading: on this data and recipe, updates beyond ~3 epochs are wasted (146-claude's -29% steps -> -79 does not extrapolate upward; the steps-to-score curve saturates near the incumbent's 2.8 epochs), and the overtrained checkpoint samples worse at T=0.8 (000's 'less-converged transfers better' reading) though RL repairs it by round 3. Data-order cost of length-homogeneous batches (002's fear) is not separable here from the overfitting; a control at the incumbent's 3,370 steps would separate them. Keep because the 3-seed mean is strictly above the incumbent's and the code is a standard 17-line batching function: the value is +60% steps at an unchanged score, to be spent on capacity (8 blocks, wider residual, or the looped 384-wide variants that lost on step count: 134/144/145) or on regularization now that the recipe overfits (EMA/SWA 131, dropout 128, label smoothing), not on more epochs. Registration c100342 committed before pods; all three pods finished ok (28/29/27 min) and were terminated by run_idea.py (exit 0). Candidate added 37 lines and deleted 6.",
